{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:56:01Z","input_tokens":2965,"cache_read_tokens":274490,"output_tokens":1551,"thinking":"Initial plan is to create a Python script utilizing PIL and NumPy for quantitative image verification. Considering previous findings, the script will avoid direct file reading of image formats such as JPG and PNG. The focus will be on implementing robust image comparison metrics.\n\n\nVerifying image dimensions, file sizes, and data types across all test frames is essential. Luminance statistics (mean, percentiles, clipping, and crush) will be checked, alongside an assessment of sharpness in the car's ROI compared to the background, and examining pixel signatures for brake thermal glow and cockpit LED indicators. This will be done to quantitatively prove the car is tack-sharp and to verify image integrity.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\nimport os, sys, glob\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image\n\ndef inspect_image(path):\n    im = Image.open(path).convert(\"RGB\")\n    w, h = im.size\n    arr = np.asarray(im, dtype=np.float32)\n    lum = 0.2126 * arr[..., 0] + 0.7152 * arr[..., 1] + 0.0722 * arr[..., 2]\n    mx = arr.max(axis=-1)\n    clip_pct = float((mx >= 253.0).mean() * 100.0)\n    dark_pct = float((mx <= 3.0).mean() * 100.0)\n    mean_l = float(lum.mean())\n    p05, p50, p95 = [float(x) for x in np.percentile(lum, [5, 50, 95])]\n\n    # Laplacian sharpness proxy: center car band vs upper background band\n    gy, gx = np.gradient(lum)\n    edge = np.hypot(gx, gy)\n    car_roi = edge[int(h * 0.35):int(h * 0.80), int(w * 0.25):int(w * 0.75)]\n    bg_roi = edge[int(h * 0.15):int(h * 0.35), int(w * 0.10):int(w * 0.90)]\n    car_sharp = float(car_roi.mean())\n    bg_sharp = float(bg_roi.mean())\n\n    # Warm red-orange glow pixels (brake glow / tail light) in lower-mid ROI\n    mid = arr[int(h * 0.30):int(h * 0.88), int(w * 0.15):int(w * 0.85)]\n    hot_px = int(((mid[..., 0] > 195) & ((mid[..., 0] - mid[..., 2]) > 115) & (mid[..., 1] < 210)).sum())\n\n    # Cockpit shift LED / LCD pixels in lower third\n    low = arr[int(h * 0.55):int(h * 0.96), int(w * 0.25):int(w * 0.75)]\n    cockpit_detail = float(edge[int(h * 0.55):int(h * 0.96), int(w * 0.25):int(w * 0.75)].mean())\n    led_px = int(((low[..., 1] > 170) & ((low[..., 1] - low[..., 0]) > 50)).sum() +\n                 ((low[..., 0] > 180) & ((low[..., 0] - low[..., 2]) > 90)).sum())\n\n    print(f\"{os.path.basename(path):32s} {w}x{h} MeanL={mean_l:5.1f} P05/50/95={p05:4.1f}/{p50:5.1f}/{p95:5.1f} \"\n          f\"Clip={clip_pct:4.2f}% Dark={dark_pct:4.1f}% Sharp(car/bg)={car_sharp:4.2f}/{bg_sharp:4.2f} \"\n          f\"HotGlowPx={hot_px:5d} LowDetail={cockpit_detail:4.2f} LEDPx={led_px:5d}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    targets = sys.argv[1:]\n    files = []\n    for t in targets:\n        if os.path.isdir(t):\n            files.extend(sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(t, \"*.jpg\"))))\n        else:\n            files.extend(sorted(glob.glob(t)))\n    for f in files:\n        inspect_image(f)\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a98b6c71-b658-48ee-9b28-e9a1c116099c\\scratch\\verify_stills_metrics.py"}}]}
